# inc-qaav4: stamp WQ_BALANCE on the weapon the character starts with, take it off and wield it again.
# Read by tools/check_alignment_drain_edges.sh. Run on a Lawful Neutral fixture (balance is not wrong for him) and a Chaotic Good fixture (it is).
#
# No balance weapon can be wished for (no lib/*.irh item carries WQ_BALANCE; the only balance
# sources are a god's gift weapon and a disabled spell). The wizard command "Add Quality to
# Weapon" (src/Debug.cpp:722) stamps a quality on the weapon in the Weapon Hand. The inventory
# manager's SPACE on the Weapon Hand puts the weapon "In the Air"; a second SPACE swaps it back,
# which is a wield (Character::Wield).
#
# Dumps: sheet-0-baseline, stamped, wielded (the message line shows "uneasy" or not), sheet-1-wielded.
s
d
@expect "Align  "
@dump:sheet-0-baseline
ESC

w
@choose "Add Quality to Weapon"
"WQ_BALANCE"
ENTER
@expect "Quality added"
@dump:stamped
i
@until ">>b)Weapon" b
SPACE
SPACE
@dump:wielded
ESC
d
@dump:sheet-1-wielded
ESC
